          "title": "You'll want to know: fūsus, fūsī",
          "segments": [
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "fūsus, fūsī — \"a spindle\"."
            },
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "Fūsus in manū ancillae celeriter vertitur. The spindle turns fast in the maid's hand."
            },
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "Second declension, masculine: fūsus, fūsī m. The weighted stick on which the spun thread is wound."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "index": 2,
          "type": "etymology",
          "title": "The word, taken apart",
          "segments": [
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "The origin of fūsus 'spindle' is not settled: Lewis & Short give the sense but no source, and EtymDB lists it without a parent. It is a different word from fūsus 'poured', from fundō."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
