              "text": "lānificium, lānificiī — \"wool-working, spinning and weaving\"."
            },
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "Lānificium in vīllā labor fēminārum est. Wool-working in the house is women's work."
            },
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "Second declension, neuter: lānificium, lānificiī n., from lāna 'wool' and faciō 'to make'. A Roman tomb often praised a woman for it."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "index": 2,
          "type": "etymology",
          "title": "The word, taken apart",
          "segments": [
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "lānificium is built on lānificus 'wool-working', from lāna 'wool' and faciō 'to make' (Lewis & Short)."
